From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMCX <noreply@openmcx.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] presence, presence_reginfo, pua, pua_reginfo,
 ims_registrar_pcscf: RFC 3680 documents and the reg event of TS 24.229

- pua_reginfo build_reginfo_full(): a contact added by a REGISTER has the
  event "registered" (RFC 3680 section 4.7.1; "created" is an administrative
  addition); no "unknown" event, which the reginfo schema does not have; no
  "received", "path" and "user_agent" attributes, which the contact element
  of the RFC 3680 schema does not have (the document was not schema-valid).
- pua_reginfo RPC commands (TS 24.229 V19.7.0):
  reginfo.shorten <usrloc domain> <AOR> <seconds> shortens every contact of
  the AOR to the given expiry and publishes one document with the event
  "shortened" (clause 5.4.1.6, network-initiated re-authentication);
  reginfo.deregister <usrloc domain> <AOR> deactivated|rejected removes every
  contact of the AOR and publishes it as terminated with that event (clause
  5.4.1.5, network-initiated deregistration). The event of the document is
  set for the usrloc callbacks of the command (reginfo_event_override).
- presence_reginfo reginfo_body_setversion(): the first document sent to a
  subscriber has the version 0 (RFC 3680 section 5.1); the presence module
  counts from 1.
- presence: an event may declare a notification body final
  (is_final_body); such a NOTIFY is sent with Subscription-State
  "terminated" and the subscription is then deleted. presence_reginfo
  declares final a document whose every registration is terminated (TS
  24.229 clause 5.4.2.1.2: "When sending a final NOTIFY request with all
  <registration> element(s) having their state attribute set to
  "terminated" ... the S-CSCF shall also terminate the subscription"). A
  terminated Subscription-State has no empty reason parameter.
- pua: the parameter refresh_before, the time before its expiry at which a
  record is refreshed (default update_period, as before), apart from the
  timer's period: the P-CSCF refreshes its reg event subscription "600
  seconds before the expiration time" (TS 24.229 clause 5.2.3); and a
  SUBSCRIBE's Expires is the requested value (10 s were added to it).
- ims_registrar_pcscf reginfo_parse_event(): every contact event of RFC
  3680; "shortened", "rejected" and "probation" were refused as unknown, so
  the P-CSCF skipped the contact of a network-initiated re-authentication or
  deregistration (TS 24.229 clauses 5.4.1.6, 5.4.1.5 and 5.2.5.2).

The modified files carry a notice of the change (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)).
---
